# You only need this file when DEPLOYING to the team's staging Firebase project —
# day-to-day development uses the local emulators and the placeholder values in
# `.env`, so most of the time you can ignore this file entirely.
# See DEPLOY.md for the full walkthrough.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.staging.local` (git-ignored — never commit real
# keys) and fill in the values your mentor gives you, or that you find at:
# Firebase console > Project settings > General > Your apps > SDK setup and configuration
#
# This is a SEPARATE Firebase project from production — its own real Auth
# users, Firestore data, and Storage bucket — so testing here never touches
# real production data. Named `.env.staging.local` on purpose: Vite only
# loads it for `npm run build:staging` (used by `deploy:preview` and
# `deploy:staging`), never for `npm run dev` or `npm run build` (which uses
# `.env.production.local` instead).
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
